       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg per day for extended-release). A dose this high greatly raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg per day), the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, with a different frequency.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses.\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is deliberate, please confirm that, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you verified the dose."
      }
